        <description>PERFORM EO.11/148(C) (ENGINEERING ORDER) REV. 00

ENGINE CHANGE UNSCHEDULED REPLACEMENT

ENGINE CHANGE UNSCHEDULED REPLACEMENT
BACKGROUND: UNSCHEDULED ENGINE CHANGE.

THIS IS A CRITICAL SYSTEMS TASK.
IF THIS TASK IS BEING ACCOMPLISHED ON BOTH ENGINES AT THE
SAME TIME THE INITIAL INSPECTION/LUBRICATION TASK MUST BE
ACCOMPLISHED BY A DIFFERENT PERSON AND A INDEPENDENT INSPECTION MUST BE
ACCOMPLISHED BY A DIFFERENT PERSON. IT IS ACCEPTABLE FOR TWO PEOPLE
TO REVERSE THEIR ROLES IN THIS INSTANCE WHEREBY THE PERSON WHO DOES
THE INITIAL TASK ON ONE ENGINE MAY DO THE INDEPENDENT INSPECTION ON THE
SECOND ENGINE AND VICE-VERSA.

ACTION:
1. AS PER RA810 AND AMM 71-00-02 REMOVE ESN 961788.  


2. RECORD THE P/N &amp; S/N OF THE ENGINE STAND/CRADLE THAT THE REMOVED ENGINE WAS PLACED ON.

STAND:     P/N:________________    S/N:________________
CRADLE:    P/N:________________    S/N:________________


3.CLOSE THE VBV DOORS (BY ACTUATING THE VSVS TO FULLY OPEN)IAW AMM TASK 72-00-00-200-804-F00 SECTION F(5).COVER THE VBV ACCESS PANELS USING MOISTURE BARRIER TAPE 3M471-2

4. CONFIRM IF THE ENGINE HAS BEEN REMOVED AN SERVICEABLE OR UNSERVICEABLE CONDITION.
   _______________________________________________________________

NOTE: IF THE ENGINE IS REMOVED UNSERVICEABLE, INSTALL AN
      UNSERVICEABLE LABEL ON THE ENGINE.
 IF THE ENGINE HAS BEEN REMOVED SERVICEABLE, CREATE A FORM 1 IAW MOE 2.16 FOLLOWING RECEIPT OF RA377 FROM TECHNICAL SERVICES, A COPY OF THE FORM 1 IS TO BE EMAILED TO POWERPLANTENGINEERING@RYANAIR.COM.

5. INSPECT AND CONFIRM THE AFT ENGINE MOUNT CENTRE LINK ASSEMBLY IS INSTALLED CORRECTLY IAW ASB 737-71A1462 REV 03 AS MANDATED BY AD 2011-18-10.

PLEASE INCLUDE ONE OF THE FOLLOWING CLOSING STATEMENT WHEN CERTIFYING THIS WORKORDER:

"INSPECTION OF THE AFT ENGINE MOUNT CENTRE LINK ASSEMBLY CARRIED OUT IAW ASB 737-71A1462 REV.03, THE CENTRE LINK ASSEMBLY ON THE AFT ENGINE MOUNT IS INSTALLED CORRECTLY"

OR

"INSPECTION OF THE AFT ENGINE MOUNT CENTRE LINK ASSEMBLY CARRIED OUT IAW ASB 737-71A1462 REV.03, THE CENTRE LINK ASSEMBLY ON THE AFT ENGINE MOUNT WAS INSTALLED INCORRECTLY. 
RECTIFICATION CARRIED OUT ON WO ___________, CENTRE LINK ASSEMBLY ON THE AFT ENGINE IS NOW INSTALLED CORRECTLY"
 
6. AS PER RA810 AND AMM 71-00-02 INSTALL ESN 892125.

7. RECORD THE P/N &amp; S/N OF THE ENGINE STAND/CRADLE THAT THE INSTALLED ENGINE WAS REMOVED FFROM.

STAND:     P/N:________________    S/N:________________
CRADLE:    P/N:________________    S/N:________________

8. ENSURE BOTH INSTALLED ENGINES ON THIS AIRCRAFT HAVE EEC SOFTWARE
   7.B.X OR LATER INSTALLED. IF REQUIRED INSTALL PER TECH NOTICE
   73-02.

NOTE: ENSURE THAT THE EEC SOFTWARE IS IN AGREEMENT WITH THE RA160 SOFTWARE CONFIGURATION SHEET. IF IS INCORRECT AMEND ACCORDING TO INSTRUCTIONS ON RA160 SOFTWARE CONFIGURATION SHEET.

9. REMOVE THE RELATED BLADE DAMAGE CHART FROM THE RA805 (AIRCRAFT DAMAGE RECORD) AND RETURN TO TECHNICAL RECORDS. ANY CORRESPONDING DAMAGE THAT NO LONGER EXISTS AS A RESULT OF THE ENGINE CHANGE MUST HAVE ITS ENTRY CLOSED IN THE DAMAGE/REPAIR RECORD.  

10. INSTALL A NEW BLADE DAMAGE CHART TO THE RA805 AND INPUT ANY EXISTING DAMAGE/REPAIR INFORMATION AS NECESSARY (REFER TO CAME 2.9.6.2)

11. SCAN A COMPLETED COPY OF THE RA810 TO TECH RECORDS AND POWERPLANT
   AT THE FOLLOWING EMAILS:
   TECREC@RYANAIR.COM &amp; POWERPLANT@RYANAIR.COM

12. DO NOT LABEL BOOK THE ENGINE TEC RECORDS WILL ACCOMPLISH THIS

NOTE: WHEN AN ENGINE IS INSTALLED, THE COMPLETED DIRTY FINGERPRINT RA810 MUST BE SENT TO TECH RECORDS.

      WHEN AN ENGINE IS REMOVED, A SCANNED COPY OF THE RA810 MUST BE SENT TO TECH RECORDS, AND THE ORIGINAL IS TO REMAIN WITH THE ENGINE. 

**********************************************************************
NOTE: THIS WORKORDER HAS AD REQUIREMENTS, A DIRTY FINGER PRINT COPY OF THIS WORKORDER MUST BE SCANNED AND EMAILED TO AD_REVIEW@RYANAIR.COM FOR REVIEW.
**********************************************************************</description>
